#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 185 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 Delays any incoming message by the specified time. With
@block = 0 it acts like the vanilla [delay]: if a new message arrives
while the delay time has not yet expired \, the old message is discarded
and the new delay time is set from the current moment.;
#X text 240 168 A zero delay time means the message is output on the
next Pd runloop iteration (as soon as possible).;
#X text 240 208 Note: the @delay property can only be set via the right
inlet or with the [prop.set] object.;
